---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Chris Dabel"
  description="Data engineer and architect. I build the data layer AI runs on, and I build with AI while I do it."
>
  <h1>Chris Dabel</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Data engineer and architect. I build the data layer AI runs on, and I
    build with AI while I do it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Twelve years of data pipelines, warehouses, and infrastructure behind
    production analytics and ML. Most recently the founding data engineer at a
    fintech, where I owned the whole path solo: ingestion, a Snowflake medallion
    architecture, orchestration in Airflow on AWS, and the governance that let
    an LLM product see only what each tenant was entitled to. The same platform
    fed the model: a labeled corpus in the millions of rows, a harness for
    scoring candidate models against each other, and per-LLM-call cost
    analytics so nobody had to guess what the AI was spending.
  </p>

  <p>
    AI is a multiplier in my work, not a substitute for it. Agentic development
    in Claude Code, custom skills and MCP servers, RAG on Snowflake Cortex. This
    site was built that way and the source is public. Knowing where AI belongs
    in a system, and where it does not, is most of the job now.
  </p>

  <p>
    Governance is what makes the rest shippable. At the fintech that meant row
    access policies over an entitlements table, masking on free text and
    financial values, service accounts on the proper user type with rotated
    keys, and SCIM work alongside the security team. None of it is exotic. All
    of it is what an auditor asks about first, and it is what let an AI product
    touch customer data at all.
  </p>

  <p>
    I do my best work at the edge of a problem nobody has mapped yet. My
    ability to hyperfocus is the engine. Through creative writing, I keep my
    creative juices flowing. My pen is my key to innovation. I inhabit the
    ambiguity, find the structure inside it, cut out the fluff, and ship
    something people can use.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before data I was an analyst: a State Department internship in Kinshasa,
    working in French, then a global news desk. Translating between worlds is
    the oldest skill I have, and it is still what bridges the business question
    and the right technical answer.
  </p>

  <p>
    I'm looking for my next opportunity: founding or staff-level data work,
    high ambiguity, high autonomy, with leadership that values clear, competent
    communication and architectural decision-making to shape a collaborative,
    cross-functional team culture.
  </p>

